+# Contract: Command line, output streams, exit statuses
+
+**Feature**: `001-pastebin-service` | **Plan**: [../plan.md](../plan.md)
+
+## Invocation
+
+```text
+python -m pastebin serve --port PORT --data DIR
+```
+
+Requires `src/` on the module search path (e.g. `PYTHONPATH=src`). Python 3.11 or newer.
+
+| Argument | Required | Accepted | Meaning |
+|----------|----------|----------|---------|
+| `serve` | yes | the only subcommand | Start the service |
+| `--port` | yes | integer `1`…`65535` | TCP port on `127.0.0.1` |
+| `--data` | yes | filesystem path | Storage directory; created if absent, including parents |
+
+No other options exist. Nothing is configurable by environment variable.
+
+## Standard output
+
+Exactly one line, ever (FR-004, FR-044, SC-009):
+
+```text
+listening on 127.0.0.1:8765
+```
+
+Written once, after the listening socket is bound and accepting, and before the first request is
+served. The port shown is the port actually bound. Nothing else is ever written to standard output —
+no request logs, no shutdown message.
+
+## Standard error
+
+Written to only for the failures this specification names:
+
+| Occasion | Output | Exit |
+|----------|--------|------|
+| Missing, non-numeric, or out-of-range `--port`; missing `--data`; unknown or missing subcommand | `argparse` usage and a message naming the offending argument | `2` |
+| `--data` cannot be created or is not writable | one line naming the directory and the OS reason | `1` |
+| `--port` cannot be bound (in use, or privileged) | one line naming the port and the OS reason | `1` |
+| A request names a snippet whose stored record cannot be read or parsed | one line naming the snippet id and the reason (FR-038) | — (service keeps running) |
+
+No per-request lines are written for any status, including 4xx — `http.server`'s default
+`log_message`/`log_error` output is suppressed ([../research.md](../research.md) R-09).
+
+On a startup failure the ready line is never printed, so a caller that waits for it can distinguish
+"started" from "failed" without a timeout heuristic.
+
+## Exit statuses
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+|--------|---------|
+| `0` | Interrupted cleanly (`SIGINT`/`SIGTERM`) after having served |
+| `1` | Startup failure: storage unusable, or port unbindable |
+| `2` | Invalid command line (`argparse`) |
+
+## Shutdown
+
+`SIGINT` (Ctrl-C) stops `serve_forever`, closes the socket, and exits `0` without writing anything.
+In-flight requests are not drained — handler threads are daemons — which is acceptable because every
+published snippet is already `fsync`ed and linked into place before its response is sent
+([storage.md](./storage.md)), so no acknowledged publication can be lost by an abrupt stop.
